# Folkprotocol Audit Close v0
#
# Tenth experimental slice. After triage-directed repairs, it rechecks factual
# fidelity and verifies only the accepted tone repairs. It deliberately does
# not open a fresh global tone-review pass.

Expect slug
Default work_dir: /home/patrick/projects/folkprotocol

Work in {work_dir}

Parallel(3):
    Codex: """Recheck citation completeness and provenance after triage-directed
repairs to research/source-maps/{slug}/120-tone-draft.md.

Required inputs are 00-commission.md, the six source maps from 10 through 60,
70-practice-strains.md, 80-practice-assessment.md, 90-protocol-dossiers.md,
100-factual-draft.md, 120-tone-draft.md, and 133-audit-triage.md. Require 133 to
end with either `AUDIT TRIAGE COMPLETE — READY` or an exact
`AUDIT TRIAGE COMPLETE — REPAIR REQUIRED — N findings` marker.

From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input digest with exactly
`sha256sum 00-commission.md 10-reddit-forums.md 20-traditional.md
30-published-research.md 40-commercial-web.md 50-experimental-communities.md
60-practitioner-folk-web.md 70-practice-strains.md 80-practice-assessment.md
90-protocol-dossiers.md 100-factual-draft.md 120-tone-draft.md
133-audit-triage.md | sha256sum`. Write it as inputDigest in
research/source-maps/{slug}/134-citation-recheck.md. If that file ends with
`CITATION RECHECK COMPLETE` and records the same digest, leave it unchanged.

Read only the required files and existing output. Do no web research and edit
no input. Write only 134-citation-recheck.md. Work yourself; do not delegate or
start another agent workflow. Check every prose citation token and reference
entry, exact source-ID existence and expansion, numerical, preparation, and
timing claims, and survival of material qualifications. Pay particular
attention to text changed to resolve accepted findings in 133. Report only
concrete mismatches with exact phrases and source locations. If none, write
`CLEAN`. End with `CITATION RECHECK COMPLETE`.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, inherit_previous_output=false, timeout=1800

    Codex: """Recheck the substantive shape after triage-directed repairs to
research/source-maps/{slug}/120-tone-draft.md.

Required inputs are 00-commission.md, 70-practice-strains.md,
80-practice-assessment.md, 90-protocol-dossiers.md, 100-factual-draft.md,
120-tone-draft.md, and 133-audit-triage.md. Require 133 to end with either
`AUDIT TRIAGE COMPLETE — READY` or an exact
`AUDIT TRIAGE COMPLETE — REPAIR REQUIRED — N findings` marker.

From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input digest with exactly
`sha256sum 00-commission.md 70-practice-strains.md 80-practice-assessment.md
90-protocol-dossiers.md 100-factual-draft.md 120-tone-draft.md
133-audit-triage.md | sha256sum`. Write it as inputDigest in
research/source-maps/{slug}/135-content-recheck.md. If that file ends with
`CONTENT RECHECK COMPLETE` and records the same digest, leave it unchanged.

Read only the required files and existing output. Do no web research and edit
no input. Write only 135-content-recheck.md. Work yourself; do not delegate or
start another agent workflow. Check that repairs did not lose a selected
direction, source tradition, strange or thin lead, useful effect size,
population or access boundary, preparation distinction, commissioner lead, or
the difference between symptoms, function, alcohol exposure, and clearance.
Check that no repair manufactured a protocol or strengthened a scoped claim.
Do not propose new tone edits or a different page. If none, write `CLEAN`. End
with `CONTENT RECHECK COMPLETE`.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, inherit_previous_output=false, timeout=1800

    Codex: """Verify only the dispositioned tone repairs in
research/source-maps/{slug}/133-audit-triage.md against the current
120-tone-draft.md.

From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input digest with exactly
`sha256sum 120-tone-draft.md 133-audit-triage.md | sha256sum`. Write it as
inputDigest in research/source-maps/{slug}/136-tone-repair-check.md. If that
file ends with `TONE REPAIR CHECK COMPLETE` and records the same digest, leave
it unchanged.

Read only 120-tone-draft.md, 133-audit-triage.md, and the existing output. Do no
web research and edit no input. Write only 136-tone-repair-check.md. Work
yourself; do not delegate or start another agent workflow.

If 133 ends READY, record that it contains no accepted unresolved repairs. If
it ends REPAIR REQUIRED, enumerate every finding marked `accept` in 133 and
classify it `repaired` or `unresolved` in the current draft. A repair may use
different wording from the suggestion; judge whether the exact defect was
removed while the constraint named in 133 survived. Do not perform a new tone
audit, introduce a new style preference, revisit rejected findings, or inspect
phrases not covered by an accepted finding. End with `TONE REPAIRS CLEAN` only
if every accepted finding is repaired; otherwise end with
`TONE REPAIRS UNRESOLVED — N findings`. In all cases, finish with
`TONE REPAIR CHECK COMPLETE`.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, inherit_previous_output=false, timeout=1200

Then Codex: """Close the bounded audit-repair cycle for
research/source-maps/{slug}/120-tone-draft.md.

Read only 120-tone-draft.md, 133-audit-triage.md,
134-citation-recheck.md, 135-content-recheck.md,
136-tone-repair-check.md, and the existing 137-audit-closure.md. Verify all
completion markers. Verify each recheck is current by recomputing its exact
documented digest from research/source-maps/{slug}/:

- 134: `sha256sum 00-commission.md 10-reddit-forums.md 20-traditional.md
  30-published-research.md 40-commercial-web.md 50-experimental-communities.md
  60-practitioner-folk-web.md 70-practice-strains.md
  80-practice-assessment.md 90-protocol-dossiers.md 100-factual-draft.md
  120-tone-draft.md 133-audit-triage.md | sha256sum`
- 135: `sha256sum 00-commission.md 70-practice-strains.md
  80-practice-assessment.md 90-protocol-dossiers.md 100-factual-draft.md
  120-tone-draft.md 133-audit-triage.md | sha256sum`
- 136: `sha256sum 120-tone-draft.md 133-audit-triage.md | sha256sum`

The files named only in digest commands may be passed to sha256sum but must not
otherwise be read. If a recheck is stale or incomplete, report the exact file
and stop without writing.

Compute the closure input digest with exactly `sha256sum 120-tone-draft.md
133-audit-triage.md 134-citation-recheck.md 135-content-recheck.md
136-tone-repair-check.md | sha256sum`. Write it as inputDigest in
research/source-maps/{slug}/137-audit-closure.md. If a completed closure records
the same digest, leave it unchanged. Write only 137-audit-closure.md. Do no web
research, do not delegate, and do not start another agent workflow.

If 134 and 135 are CLEAN and 136 says TONE REPAIRS CLEAN, end with
`AUDIT CLOSURE COMPLETE — READY`. Otherwise account for every concrete finding
from 134 through 136 and end with
`AUDIT CLOSURE COMPLETE — REPAIR REQUIRED — N findings`. Do not add new tone
findings or reopen findings rejected in 133.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, inherit_previous_output=false, timeout=1200
